{
 "title": "Why Distance Doesn't Rule Seasons",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "Distance barely changes",
   "say": "Earth's orbit is actually almost a perfect circle. The distance only changes by about 3 percent all year!",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "dist_title",
     "x": 850,
     "y": 50,
     "text": "Distance vs. Tilt:",
     "size": 42,
     "underline": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "dist_fact1",
     "x": 850,
     "y": 115,
     "text": "• Jan (closest): 147 million km",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "dist_fact2",
     "x": 850,
     "y": 165,
     "text": "• July (farthest): 152 million km",
     "size": 32
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "dist_diff",
     "x": 850,
     "y": 215,
     "text": "Only a 3% difference — too small to drive seasons!",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Tilt points North toward the Sun",
   "say": "Look at the left position in June. The northern half of Earth tilts directly toward the sunlight.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "june_lbl",
     "x": 280,
     "y": 465,
     "text": "June (N. Summer)",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "dec_lbl",
     "x": 1320,
     "y": 465,
     "text": "Dec (N. Winter)",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "blue",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "ray1",
     "x1": 730,
     "y1": 580,
     "x2": 330,
     "y2": 580,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "ray2",
     "x1": 730,
     "y1": 620,
     "x2": 330,
     "y2": 620,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "ray_lbl",
     "x": 530,
     "y": 530,
     "text": "Direct sunlight",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Why tilt beats distance",
   "say": "Let's clear the orbit diagram and zoom in on a patch of ground to see why tilt makes such a huge difference.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "erase",
     "ids": [
      "sun",
      "sunlabel",
      "orbit",
      "orbitlabel",
      "earth1",
      "axis1",
      "earth2",
      "axis2",
      "earth3",
      "axis3",
      "earth4",
      "axis4",
      "june_lbl",
      "dec_lbl",
      "ray1",
      "ray2",
      "ray_lbl"
     ]
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "two_reasons",
     "x": 60,
     "y": 250,
     "text": "Tilting toward the Sun gives two huge boosts:",
     "size": 38,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Effect 1: Concentrated vs. Spread Out",
   "say": "First: direct light hits high overhead and concentrates heat into a small area. Low-angle winter light spreads the same energy over a much wider area.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eff1_title",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 330,
     "text": "1. Concentrated Sunlight (Summer)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "ground1",
     "x1": 100,
     "y1": 560,
     "x2": 600,
     "y2": 560,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 6
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "s_ray1",
     "x1": 300,
     "y1": 400,
     "x2": 300,
     "y2": 550,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "s_ray2",
     "x1": 400,
     "y1": 400,
     "x2": 400,
     "y2": 550,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "spot1",
     "cx": 350,
     "cy": 560,
     "rx": 65,
     "ry": 15,
     "color": "red",
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "spot1_lbl",
     "x": 350,
     "y": 590,
     "text": "Small area = Intense heat",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eff2_title",
     "x": 850,
     "y": 330,
     "text": "Low-Angle Sunlight (Winter)",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "ground2",
     "x1": 850,
     "y1": 560,
     "x2": 1450,
     "y2": 560,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 6
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "w_ray1",
     "x1": 880,
     "y1": 400,
     "x2": 1080,
     "y2": 550,
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "w_ray2",
     "x1": 1030,
     "y1": 400,
     "x2": 1280,
     "y2": 550,
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 5,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "spot2",
     "cx": 1180,
     "cy": 560,
     "rx": 140,
     "ry": 15,
     "color": "blue",
     "fill": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "spot2_lbl",
     "x": 1180,
     "y": 590,
     "text": "Spread out = Weak heat",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "blue",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Effect 2: Longer Daylight Hours",
   "say": "Second: tilting toward the Sun keeps you in the sunlit half for more hours each day, giving the ground much more time to warm up!",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "summary_box",
     "x": 80,
     "y": 670,
     "w": 1370,
     "h": 160,
     "color": "green",
     "width": 4,
     "fill": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "eff_days",
     "x": 110,
     "y": 690,
     "text": "2. Longer Days: ~15 hours of heating in summer vs. ~9 hours in winter.",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "conclusion",
     "x": 110,
     "y": 755,
     "text": "Takeaway: Steep angle + Long days easily overpower the tiny 3% distance change!",
     "size": 34,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}